<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Total-conversion behavior, GAMEPLAY-DATABASE half.

  This file may only ever touch Gameplay-database tables. It is wired to
  InGameActions ONLY in Warmstone.modinfo. Its Configuration-database
  counterpart is Warmstone_HideVanillaLeaders_Config.xml, which carries the full
  explanation of why the two must not be combined into one file.

  Short version: the previous single-file version put `Players` (Configuration)
  and `CivilizationLeaders` (Gameplay) together and loaded it into both
  databases, so each pass hit a table that does not exist in it and aborted the
  whole file. The Configuration-side failure is what left every vanilla leader in
  the picker. The Gameplay-side failure had never been observed because no game
  was ever actually started - it would have failed the same way, on
  "no such table: Players".

  `CivilizationLeaders` is the LeaderType<->CivilizationType pairing table. This
  is the more surgical target than the `Civilizations`/`Leaders` catalog tables:
  vanilla civ and leader data (Civilopedia entries, AI logic, art) stays intact,
  only the pairing that makes them selectable goes away. Confirmed against
  Base/Assets/Gameplay/Data/Schema/01_GameplaySchema.sql that no other gameplay
  table carries a foreign key back to CivilizationLeaders, so a bare delete
  leaves no dangling references.

  Load order: the action for this file runs at LoadOrder 100, after all DLC
  gameplay data, and each Warmstone civ's own files run later still (110+) so
  their own CivilizationLeaders rows are added after this delete rather than
  being wiped by it.
-->
<GameInfo>
	<CivilizationLeaders>
		<Delete/>
		<Row CivilizationType="CIVILIZATION_ROME" LeaderType="LEADER_TRAJAN" CapitalName="LOC_CITY_NAME_ROME"/>
	</CivilizationLeaders>
</GameInfo>
